{#
    The signed-out layout's brand panel: the mark, the instance's name, and
    what Renovo does.

    The name is `instance_name` rather than a wordmark, as in the rail: the
    operator may have called the instance something else, and theirs is the
    name that belongs over their sign-in form.

    The pitch is careful not to promise what the application does not keep. It
    names no channel — there are eleven, and the list will change — and it
    says the data stays on this server, not that nothing leaves it: exchange
    rates are fetched and reminders are sent.

    Below 900px the stylesheet reduces the panel to the mark and the name, so
    on a phone the form is the first thing on the screen; the pitch is still in
    the page for a screen reader, which reads the panel as a complementary
    landmark before the form.
#}
<aside class="auth-brand" aria-label="{{ instance_name }}">
    <div class="auth-brand-head">
        <svg class="brand-mark auth-mark" viewBox="0 0 460 427" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <use href="#renovo-mark"></use>
        </svg>
        <div>
            <p class="auth-instance">{{ instance_name }}</p>
            <p class="auth-tagline">{{ t('shell.tagline') }}</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="auth-pitch">
        <p class="auth-pitch-title">{{ t('auth_brand.pitch') }}</p>

        <ul class="auth-points">
            {% for point in [
                {'icon': 'household', 'key': 'household'},
                {'icon': 'currency', 'key': 'currency'},
                {'icon': 'notifications', 'key': 'reminders'}
            ] %}
                <li class="auth-point">
                    <span class="auth-point-icon">{{ icon(point.icon) }}</span>
                    <span>
                        <span class="auth-point-title">{{ t('auth_brand.' ~ point.key ~ '_title') }}</span>
                        <span class="auth-point-body">{{ t('auth_brand.' ~ point.key ~ '_body') }}</span>
                    </span>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="auth-brand-foot">{{ t('auth_brand.footer') }}</p>
</aside>
